[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create the detailed report:\n\n## Web UI Architecture Exploration - Comprehensive Report\n\nI've completed a thorough exploration of the `packages/web-ui/` SvelteKit project and related daemon API routes. Here's what I found:\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overall SvelteKit Project Structure\n\n**Location**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/web-ui/`\n\n```\npackages/web-ui/\n├── src/\n│   ├── routes/                 # SvelteKit routing\n│   │   ├── +layout.svelte      # Root layout with app initialization\n│   │   ├── +page.svelte        # Dashboard home page\n│   │   ├── tasks/+page.svelte  # Tasks page with detail panel\n│   │   ├── items/+page.svelte  # Spec items page\n│   │   ├── inbox/+page.svelte  # Inbox page\n│   │   └── observations/+page.svelte\n│   ├── lib/\n│   │   ├── api.ts              # Main API client (daemon/static dispatch)\n│   │   ├── api-static.ts       # Static mode fallback API\n│   │   ├── constants.ts        # Daemon port/URL constants\n│   │   ├── stores/\n│   │   │   ├── mode.svelte.ts  # Mode detection (daemon vs static)\n│   │   │   ├── project.svelte.ts # Multi-project selection\n│   │   │   ├── connection.svelte.ts # WebSocket connection state\n│   │   │   └── taskDetail.svelte.ts # Task detail panel store\n│   │   ├── websocket/\n│   │   │   ├── manager.ts      # WebSocketManager with reconnect logic\n│   │   │   └── types.ts        # Connection state types\n│   │   ├── components/\n│   │   │   ├── ui/             # Shadcn/bits-ui components (accordion, badge, button, card, dialog, etc.)\n│   │   │   ├── ReadOnlyBanner.svelte # Static mode indicator\n│   │   │   ├── Sidebar.svelte  # Main navigation sidebar\n│   │   │   ├── ProjectSelector.svelte # Multi-project selector\n│   │   │   ├── ConnectionStatus.svelte # WS connection badge\n│   │   │   ├── CommandPalette.svelte # Global command/search\n│   │   │   └── TaskFilters.svelte\n│   │   ├── types/\n│   │   │   └── snapshot.ts     # Static export snapshot types\n│   │   └── assets/\n│   ├── app.css                 # Tailwind + CSS vars (oklch colors)\n│   └── app.d.ts\n├── svelte.config.js            # SvelteKit config (static adapter for GitHub Pages)\n├── package.json                # Dependencies\n└── [build output: build/]\n```\n\n**Framework Stack**:\n- **SvelteKit 2.49.1** with Svelte 5.45.6\n- **Tailwind CSS 4.1.18** with PostCSS\n- **Bits-ui 2.15.4** (headless components)\n- **Lucide Svelte icons**\n- **@tanstack/table-core** for data tables\n- **Playwright** for E2E testing\n- **Static adapter** for GitHub Pages deployment\n\n---\n\n## 2. How Existing Pages Are Structured\n\nAll pages follow a consistent pattern using Svelte 5 runes (`$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`):\n\n### **Example: Tasks Page** (`/routes/tasks/+page.svelte`)\n- **AC References**: @web-dashboard ac-4, ac-5, ac-9, ac-10, ac-33 (task filtering, detail view, WebSocket updates)\n- **Pattern**:\n  1. **State**: `tasks`, `total`, `loading`, `panel.open`, `panel.task`, filters\n  2. **Reactivity**: `$effect` blocks on URL params, project version, ref query param\n  3. **Data Loading**: `fetchTasks()` called on mount and when filters change\n  4. **WebSocket**: Subscribes to `'tasks'` topic on mount, unsubscribes on destroy\n  5. **Detail Panel**: Right-side modal overlay showing selected task with notes, todos, actions\n  6. **Actions**: Start task, add notes (disabled in static mode)\n\n### **Example: Inbox Page** (`/routes/inbox/+page.svelte`)\n- **AC References**: @web-dashboard ac-16-19, @gh-pages-export ac-17-18 (static mode support)\n- **Pattern**:\n  1. Inline add-item form (hidden in static mode)\n  2. Optimistic UI updates (add/delete local before reload)\n  3. Graceful static mode with `ReadOnlyModeError` catch\n  4. Relative time formatting (just now, 5m ago, etc.)\n  5. Confirmation dialog for destructive actions\n\n### **Key Page Patterns**:\n- **Mount/Lifecycle**: Load data in `onMount()`, set up subscriptions\n- **Reactivity**: Use `$effect` for URL params, project version changes, session updates\n- **Error Handling**: Try/catch with user-friendly messages\n- **Static Mode Awareness**: Check `isStaticMode()` before write operations\n- **Accessibility**: ARIA labels, semantic HTML, keyboard support\n\n---\n\n## 3. API Client in lib/ (api.ts)\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/web-ui/src/lib/api.ts`\n\n**Architecture**: Mode-aware dispatch that switches between live daemon and static JSON:\n\n```typescript\n// Pattern for all read operations:\nexport async function fetchTasks(params?: ...): Promise<PaginatedResponse<TaskSummary>> {\n  if (isStaticMode()) {\n    return fetchTasksStatic(params);  // Use embedded JSON\n  }\n  // Otherwise fetch from daemon with X-Kspec-Dir header\n  const response = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/tasks`, {\n    headers: getProjectHeaders()  // Includes X-Kspec-Dir for multi-project\n  });\n  if (!response.ok) await handleResponseError(response);\n  return response.json();\n}\n\n// Pattern for write operations:\nexport async function startTask(ref: string): Promise<void> {\n  assertWritable('start task');  // Throws ReadOnlyModeError in static mode\n  const response = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/tasks/${ref}/start`, {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: getProjectHeaders()\n  });\n  if (!response.ok) await handleResponseError(response);\n}\n```\n\n**Main Functions**:\n- **Fetch**: `fetchTasks()`, `fetchTask()`, `fetchItems()`, `fetchItem()`, `fetchItemTasks()`, `fetchInbox()`, `fetchSessionContext()`, `fetchObservations()`, `search()`\n- **Write**: `startTask()`, `addTaskNote()`, `addInboxItem()`, `deleteInboxItem()` (all disabled in static mode)\n- **Project Header**: `getProjectHeaders()` injects `X-Kspec-Dir: {projectPath}` for multi-directory daemon support\n- **Error Handling**: `handleResponseError()` detects invalid project errors and clears selection\n- **Constants**: `DAEMON_API_BASE = \"http://localhost:3456\"`\n\n---\n\n## 4. WebSocket Integration\n\n**Location**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/`\n\n### **WebSocketManager** (`manager.ts`)\nFull lifecycle management with exponential backoff:\n\n```typescript\nclass WebSocketManager {\n  // Connection\n  connect()           // Opens WebSocket with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s)\n  disconnect()        // Clean shutdown\n  setProjectPath()    // Reconnect with different project (multi-directory support)\n  \n  // Subscriptions\n  subscribe(topics: string[])    // Send subscribe command and track locally\n  unsubscribe(topics: string[])  // Remove subscription\n  on(topic, handler)             // Register event handler\n  off(topic, handler)            // Unregister handler\n  \n  // State\n  getState(): ConnectionState    // 'disconnected' | 'connecting' | 'connected' | 'reconnecting'\n  isConnected()\n  isConnectionLost()             // Returns true after 10s disconnected\n  getStats()                     // { connect_count, reconnect_count, last_connected_at, ... }\n  getSubscriptions()\n}\n```\n\n**Key Features**:\n- **Exponential Backoff**: Reconnect attempts at 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s, 30s (capped), max 10 attempts\n- **Sequence Deduplication**: Tracks `lastSeqProcessed` to skip duplicate messages (reset on reconnect)\n- **Re-subscription**: Automatically re-subscribes to all topics after reconnect (AC-32)\n- **Connection Lost Indicator**: State change events after 10s without connection (AC-29)\n- **Project Path Support**: Query parameter for multi-directory daemon (AC-34)\n- **Message Types**:\n  - `ConnectedEvent`: Initial connection confirmation with session ID\n  - `BroadcastEvent`: Data updates with msg_id, seq, topic, data\n  - `CommandAck`: Response to subscribe/unsubscribe commands\n\n### **Connection Store** (`connection.svelte.ts`)\nGlobal state wrapper using Svelte runes:\n\n```typescript\nexport function initConnection(options?: WebSocketManagerOptions): void\nexport function reconnectWithProject(projectPath: string | null): void\nexport function getConnectionState(): ConnectionState\nexport function isConnectionLost(): boolean\nexport function isConnected(): boolean\nexport function subscribe(topics: string[]): void\nexport function on(topic: string, handler: (event: any) => void): void\n// Similar: unsubscribe, off, disconnect, getStats, getSubscriptions\n```\n\n**Usage in Pages**:\n```javascript\n// In +page.svelte mount:\nonMount(() => {\n  subscribe(['tasks']);  // Ask for updates on 'tasks' topic\n  on('tasks', handleTaskUpdate);  // Register handler\n});\n\nonDestroy(() => {\n  off('tasks', handleTaskUpdate);\n  unsubscribe(['tasks']);\n});\n\n// Handler receives BroadcastEvent:\nfunction handleTaskUpdate(event: BroadcastEvent) {\n  console.log(event.topic, event.data);  // e.g. 'tasks', { ulid: '...', ... }\n  loadTasks();  // Reload list\n  updateHighlight(event.data.ulid);  // 3s highlight animation\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Static Mode Handling\n\n**Location**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/web-ui/src/lib/stores/mode.svelte.ts`\n\n### **Mode Detection Flow**:\n1. **Build-time flag**: `VITE_STATIC_MODE=true` env var (skips daemon check entirely)\n2. **Runtime daemon check**: Try health check at `http://localhost:3456/health` (2s timeout)\n3. **Fallback to static JSON**: Fetch `kspec-snapshot.json` from build output (5s timeout)\n4. **Error fallback**: Stay in daemon mode if nothing available (let error handler show message)\n\n```typescript\nexport async function initMode(): Promise<void> {\n  if (BUILD_STATIC_MODE) {  // AC-19: Build flag override\n    await loadStaticSnapshot();\n    return;\n  }\n  // Try daemon health check...\n  // Fall back to static JSON from ${base}/kspec-snapshot.json (AC-20: respects BASE_PATH)\n  // Default to daemon mode if neither available\n}\n\nexport function isStaticMode(): boolean {\n  return BUILD_STATIC_MODE || mode === 'static';  // Synchronous (no race conditions)\n}\n```\n\n### **Static API** (`api-static.ts`)\nMirrors the main API but reads from `KspecSnapshot`:\n\n```typescript\n// Read operations return filtered/paginated snapshot data\nexport function fetchTasksStatic(params?: ...): PaginatedResponse<TaskSummary>\nexport function fetchTaskStatic(ref: string): TaskDetail | null\nexport function fetchItemsStatic(params?: ...): PaginatedResponse<ItemSummary>\n// ... similar for items, inbox, session, observations, search\n\n// Write operations throw ReadOnlyModeError\nexport function startTaskStatic(_ref: string): never {\n  throw new ReadOnlyModeError('start task');\n}\n```\n\n### **Snapshot Structure** (`types/snapshot.ts`):\n```typescript\ninterface KspecSnapshot {\n  version: string;\n  exported_at: string;  // ISO timestamp for AC-15 freshness indicator\n  project: { name, version, description };\n  tasks: ExportedTask[];        // Extends TaskDetail\n  items: ExportedItem[];        // Extends ItemDetail with children, inherited_acs\n  inbox: InboxItem[];\n  session: SessionContext | null;\n  observations: Observation[];\n  agents: Agent[];\n  workflows: Workflow[];\n  conventions: Convention[];\n  validation?: ExportedValidation;  // AC-14: validation badge\n}\n```\n\n### **Component Integration**:\n- **ReadOnlyBanner.svelte**: Shows amber banner with export timestamp and validation badge (AC-15, AC-14)\n- **All write operations**: Wrapped in try/catch for `ReadOnlyModeError`, show user-friendly message\n- **URL detection**: Pages show `?ref=task-slug` for deep linking in both modes\n- **Graceful degradation**: Disabled buttons with tooltips in static mode (AC-16)\n\n---\n\n## 6. UI Components and Styling Patterns\n\n**Styling**:\n- **Tailwind CSS 4.1.18** with postcss\n- **CSS variables** in OKLCH color space (accessible, device-independent)\n- **Dark mode support** via `.dark` class\n- **Responsive**: Mobile-first with `md:` and `lg:` breakpoints\n- **Component library**: Shadcn/bits-ui (accordion, badge, button, card, command, data-table, dialog, input, select, separator, sheet, sidebar, skeleton, table, tabs, textarea, tooltip)\n\n**Common Patterns**:\n```svelte\n<!-- Buttons with variants -->\n<Button variant=\"default\" | \"secondary\" | \"destructive\" | \"outline\" | \"ghost\">\n<Button size=\"sm\" | \"default\" | \"lg\">\n\n<!-- Badges for status -->\n<Badge class=\"bg-blue-500\">In Progress</Badge>\n\n<!-- Card layouts -->\n<Card>\n  <CardHeader><CardTitle>...</CardTitle></CardHeader>\n  <CardContent>...</CardContent>\n</Card>\n\n<!-- Forms -->\n<Input placeholder=\"...\" />\n<Textarea rows={3} />\n<Select>...</Select>\n\n<!-- Modals -->\n<Dialog bind:open={isOpen}>\n  <DialogContent>\n    <DialogHeader><DialogTitle>...</DialogTitle></DialogHeader>\n    ...\n  </DialogContent>\n</Dialog>\n\n<!-- Tooltips -->\n<Tooltip.Root>\n  <Tooltip.Trigger>{snippet child({ props })}</Tooltip.Trigger>\n  <Tooltip.Content>Help text</Tooltip.Content>\n</Tooltip.Root>\n```\n\n**Key Components**:\n- **Sidebar**: Desktop navigation, project selector, session focus, observations badge\n- **MobileNav**: Mobile bottom navigation (hidden on desktop)\n- **ConnectionStatus**: Badge showing WS state (Connected | Connecting | Disconnected | Connection Lost)\n- **ReadOnlyBanner**: Amber banner with export time and validation status\n- **ProjectSelector**: Dropdown to switch between registered projects\n- **CommandPalette**: Global search/command (Cmd+K)\n- **TaskFilters**: Status/type/tag filter UI\n\n---\n\n## 7. Layout Structure\n\n**Root Layout** (`+layout.svelte`):\n```svelte\n<script>\n  onMount(async () => {\n    // 1. Detect mode (daemon or static)\n    await initMode();\n    \n    // 2. In static mode: skip projects + WebSocket\n    if (isStaticMode()) return;\n    \n    // 3. In daemon mode: load projects + connect WebSocket\n    await loadProjects();\n    const projectPath = getSelectedProjectPath();\n    initConnection({ projectPath });\n  });\n</script>\n\n<SidebarProvider>\n  <Sidebar />          <!-- Hidden on mobile with md:block -->\n  <SidebarInset>\n    <ReadOnlyBanner /> <!-- Only in static mode -->\n    <main>\n      {#if ready}\n        {@render children()}\n      {/if}\n    </main>\n  </SidebarInset>\n  <MobileNav />        <!-- Hidden on desktop -->\n</SidebarProvider>\n```\n\n**Routes**:\n- `/` - Dashboard with task counts by status (clickable)\n- `/tasks` - Full task list with filters + inline detail panel\n- `/items` - Spec items list\n- `/inbox` - Inbox with add form\n- `/observations` - Observations with filtering\n\n---\n\n## 8. Store/State Management Patterns\n\n**Svelte 5 Runes** (reactive without imports):\n```javascript\n// Reactive state\nlet count = $state(0);\nlet items = $state<Task[]>([]);\n\n// Derived values\nlet doubled = $derived(count * 2);\nlet byStatus = $derived.by(() => {\n  // Expensive computation only when dependencies change\n  return groupBy(items, 'status');\n});\n\n// Effects (replace onMount/onDestroy)\n$effect(() => {\n  const version = getProjectVersion();  // Dependency\n  if (version > 0) loadData();  // Auto-reruns when version changes\n});\n```\n\n**Store Files**:\n\n1. **mode.svelte.ts** - App-wide mode (daemon/static)\n   - `initMode()`, `isStaticMode()`, `getSnapshot()`, `getExportedAt()`\n   - `getSnapshotValidation()`, `assertWritable()`\n\n2. **project.svelte.ts** - Multi-project selection\n   - `loadProjects()`, `selectProject()`, `getSelectedProjectPath()`\n   - `hasMultipleProjects()`, `getProjectVersion()` (for triggering reloads)\n   - `isInvalidProjectError()` (for detecting 400/404 with specific messages)\n\n3. **connection.svelte.ts** - WebSocket connection state\n   - `initConnection()`, `reconnectWithProject()`, `getConnectionState()`\n   - `isConnected()`, `isConnectionLost()`\n   - `subscribe()`, `on()`, `off()`, `unsubscribe()`\n\n4. **taskDetail.svelte.ts** - Task detail panel (legacy store wrapper)\n   - Used for backward compatibility; pages now use `$state` directly\n\n---\n\n## 9. Triage Daemon API Routes\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/routes/triage.ts`\n\n**Endpoints**:\n```\nGET    /api/triage                    # List with status/action filters, sorted by created_at desc\nGET    /api/triage/export             # Export records as JSON or context (format= param)\nPOST   /api/triage                    # Record triage decision\nGET    /api/triage/:ref               # Get single record\nPOST   /api/triage/:ref/override      # Override decision (allows re-acting)\nPOST   /api/triage/:ref/act           # Execute action (promote/delete/defer/spec-gap/duplicate)\n```\n\n**Key Features**:\n- **Valid Actions**: `promote` (create task), `delete` (remove inbox), `defer` (no-op), `spec-gap` (create observation), `duplicate` (remove)\n- **Status Flow**: `pending` → `triaged` → `acted_on` (or `override` to re-triage)\n- **Export Format**: JSON or `context` format (shared with `exportTriageRecords`)\n- **Error Codes**:\n  - `404`: Not found (inbox item or record)\n  - `409`: Already acted on (can't act twice)\n  - `422`: Pending record without decision (can't act without triaging first)\n- **WebSocket Broadcast**: Publishes `triage:updates` topic with events:\n  - `triage_record_created`, `triage_record_updated`, `triage_record_acted`\n\n**Execution Logic** (lines 62-114):\n```typescript\nasync function executeTriageAction(record, ctx) {\n  switch (record.action) {\n    case 'promote':\n      // Create task from item_snapshot, return task ref\n    case 'delete' | 'duplicate':\n      // Delete inbox item\n    case 'defer':\n      // No-op\n    case 'spec-gap':\n      // Create observation with question type\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Response Format** (AC-trait-api-endpoint):\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"record\": {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01...\",\n    \"inbox_ref\": \"01...\",\n    \"item_snapshot\": \"original inbox text\",\n    \"status\": \"triaged\",\n    \"action\": \"promote\",\n    \"reasoning\": \"...\",\n    \"decided_by\": \"user\",\n    \"evidence_refs\": [\"@ref1\", \"@ref2\"],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-22T...\",\n    \"override_reasoning\": null,\n    \"override_by\": null,\n    \"acted_at\": null,\n    \"result_ref\": null\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. Key Implementation Insights\n\n### **Multi-Directory Support** (AC: @multi-directory-daemon)\n- **API Header**: `X-Kspec-Dir: /path/to/project` injected by `getProjectHeaders()`\n- **Project Selection**: Sidebar dropdown shows registered projects\n- **Project Change Trigger**: `getProjectVersion()` incremented when selected, pages watch it with `$effect`\n- **WebSocket**: Project path as query param: `ws://localhost:3456/ws?project=/path`\n- **Error Recovery**: Invalid project errors (400/404) clear selection and show error\n\n### **Static Mode** (AC: @gh-pages-export)\n- **No Daemon Dependency**: Works fully offline with embedded JSON snapshot\n- **Graceful Degradation**: Write operations throw `ReadOnlyModeError` with user message\n- **Deep Linking**: `?ref=task-slug` resolved from snapshot both ways\n- **Data Freshness**: \"Data as of: 2h ago\" with relative time formatting\n- **Validation Badge**: Shows error count if snapshot has validation issues\n- **Base Path Support**: Respects SvelteKit `base` for GitHub Pages (set via `BASE_PATH` env)\n\n### **Real-time Updates** (AC: @web-dashboard ac-33)\n- **Topic Subscription**: Pages subscribe on mount (`subscribe(['tasks'])`)\n- **Event Handlers**: Registered per topic (`on('tasks', handler)`)\n- **Highlight Animation**: Updated task IDs marked with Set, removed after 3s\n- **Dual Update**: Reload list + reload detail if selected task updated\n\n### **Session Management**\n- **Focus**: Current work focus displayed in sidebar (readonly)\n- **Observations**: Unresolved count badge in sidebar nav\n- **30s Polling**: Session data refreshed periodically (will be replaced with WebSocket)\n- **Project-aware**: Reloads when project changes\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Files\n\n| File | Purpose | Key Functions |\n|------|---------|---------------|\n| `/lib/api.ts` | Main API client | `fetchTasks()`, `startTask()`, mode dispatch |\n| `/lib/api-static.ts` | Static fallback | `fetchTasksStatic()`, `searchStatic()` |\n| `/lib/stores/mode.svelte.ts` | Mode detection | `initMode()`, `isStaticMode()`, snapshot loading |\n| `/lib/stores/project.svelte.ts` | Project selection | `loadProjects()`, `selectProject()`, version tracking |\n| `/lib/stores/connection.svelte.ts` | WebSocket state | `initConnection()`, `subscribe()`, `on()` |\n| `/lib/websocket/manager.ts` | WebSocket lifecycle | Reconnect, dedupe, re-subscribe, project support |\n| `/routes/+layout.svelte` | Root layout | App init, mode detection, sidebar/nav |\n| `/routes/+page.svelte` | Dashboard | Task counts by status, clickable cards |\n| `/routes/tasks/+page.svelte` | Tasks list + detail | Filters, WebSocket updates, inline panel |\n| `/routes/inbox/+page.svelte` | Inbox | Add/delete items, confirmation dialogs |\n| `/lib/components/ReadOnlyBanner.svelte` | Static indicator | Freshness time, validation badge |\n| `/daemon/routes/triage.ts` | Triage API | List, record, override, act, export |\n\nAll files are **production-ready** with comprehensive AC coverage, error handling, and accessibility support."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a8a07ef (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 79550\ntool_uses: 31\nduration_ms: 89429</usage>"}]